\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch {The tires crunched back onto gravel, the forest thinning into the familiar slopes of the Weshaven road. I risked a glance at Mom\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 her skirt was streaked brown at the hem, her shoes the same. She did not look happy. If looks could kill, I\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d be the one in the trunk with the carcass.}
\par\plain {In the middle seat beside me was the mage. Glover? Rover? Clover? Right\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 Clover. Maybe. Names and I don\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t get along, especially when I thought I was about to get mugged a few minutes ago.}
\par\plain {The ride was worse than the silence before. Four Hunters crammed into the truck bed, all pressed against a massive monster carcass I should\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92ve been able to identify if I\u8217\'92d ever paid attention during }{\f0\fs24\i1 Studies of Arcane Creatures}{. Spoiler: I didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93So, um.\u8221\'94 I cleared my throat, shooting a glance at not-Rover. \u8220\'93Why are you guys here?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Collecting bounty.\u8221\'94 Her voice was flat, like it was the most boring thing in the world. \u8220\'93Killing monsters. That sort of stuff.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Monsters, huh.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {From the back, the huntress snorted. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Aye. Mayor\u8217\'92s been bleedin\u8217\'92 about beasts turnin\u8217\'92 up more\u8217\'92n usual. Paladins won\u8217\'92t come this far out, so they post coin\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 and here we are.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Didn\u8217\'92t one of the council folk say they brought in some expert from Edenfield?\u8221\'94 Rowan asked, wiping blood off his hands with a rag. \u8220\'93Supposedly somethin\u8217\'92 big\u8217\'92s been movin\u8217\'92 this way.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {Owen scoffed without even looking up from the carcass. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What good\u8217\'92s a posh twat from Edenfield gonna do? Monsters don\u8217\'92t die from books.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Excuse me,\u8221\'94 Mom snapped suddenly, her voice like a whip. \u8220\'93But you are a guest in my car. You will mind your manners.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {The silence after that was deafening. Even the road noise seemed to back off.}
\par\plain {Finally, Clover turned to me. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re local. Where are you from?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93The old lighthouse,\u8221\'94 I said, keeping my eyes on the road. \u8220\'93By the cliff.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93There\u8217\'92s no guards out that way,\u8221\'94 she said, studying me. \u8220\'93You\u8217\'92ll be all right?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {Before I could answer, Mom cut in. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93We\u8217\'92re fine. I\u8217\'92ve set up a secure perimeter. Nothing gets past the ring.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {Clover tilted her head, almost like she was testing something. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Ah. So it\u8217\'92s true\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 those kinds are in this part of the country.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {I could feel Mom\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s glare before she even spoke. \u8220\'93Do you have a problem with that?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93None at all, ma\u8217\'92am,\u8221\'94 Clover said smoothly.}
