\par\plain 
\par\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch {The gravel crunched to a halt in front of the Weshaven Town Hall, the truck wheezing like it had run the whole way on nerves instead of fuel.}
\par\plain {Fredrick hopped down from the bed, armor clanking, halberd slung casual over his shoulder. He flashed me that same too-easy grin. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Thank you for the ride, dear friend. And my apologies if you felt\u8230\'85 threatened during our meeting. Had we not pressed the point, we might\u8217\'92ve waited another hour for another car.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yeah, I get it.\u8221\'94 I shifted in the driver\u8217\'92s seat, gripping the wheel tighter than I meant to. \u8220\'93But maybe next time, try asking nicely. You\u8217\'92re lucky my mother didn\u8217\'92t turn you into frogs.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {Clover, climbing down after him, froze mid-step. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93She could do that?\u8221\'94 she whispered.}
\par\plain {Mom leaned over from the passenger side, her voice cool as stone. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Do you want to find out?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {Clover didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t say another word.}
\par\plain {Fredrick chuckled, unfazed, and reached into his satchel. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Anyhow, friends\u8230\'85\u8221\'94 He produced two cards, stiff parchment with gilded edges. \u8220\'93We\u8217\'92ll be in Weshaven a few months, until this monster situation resolves. Should you require our services, I\u8217\'92d be open to accepting bounties directly.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {I took the card, turning it over like it might bite me. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93\u8230\'85Thanks,\u8221\'94 I muttered, because what else do you say to people who drop dead monsters in the back of your mom\u8217\'92s truck?}
\par\plain {Fredrick tipped his head, all charm and menace rolled into one. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Stay safe, friends. May the wind keep you safe.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {I only managed a nod and a half-hearted wave before I hit the gas. The truck lurched forward, coughing smoke.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What a bunch of fucking weirdos,\u8221\'94 I breathed.}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Language, Edward,\u8221\'94 Mom said without missing a beat.}
